F. sympy: the one-loop K_alpha takes alpha(0) exactly
  [ok] d ln alpha(0)/d ln m == -alpha(0) d(alpha^-1(0))/d ln m (identity)
   so with a one-loop threshold d(alpha^-1)/d ln m = -b/(2 pi) (alpha-independent),
   the input alpha in 43 alpha/(54 pi) is alpha(0): the CODATA (Thomson-limit) value.

